n also see that with  the wattage that is used when we're  using the graphics we're not hitting the  60 watts that Apple talked about and  because of that the performance doesn't  match up to like an RTX 3080 if they  showed off on screen so should you wait  for the three nanometer chips what  difference will that make and what  features will we get well first off we  know that it's not going to come out in  early January or February it's going to  be mid-march so that's a long wait and  with that one thing we're going to see  are lower temperatures now the 16 inch  didn't have that many issues with  thermals except for in one instance  where the 24 query mode Max would  actually beat out the 32 core in a 16  inch other than that though it was fine  but the 14 inch a 32 core M1 Max would  actually run slower if you really push  it compared to a 16 inch base model now  three nanometer is going to use a lot  less power it's going to have less heat  so we're gonna have less thermal  throttling and better performance now on  the other side what we're going to have  is better battery life if you take a  look at that 16 inch with M1 Max it  drains a ton of power when we're pushing  all of those cores and three nanometer  is a lot more efficient now with that  this MacBook the reason I'm not always  happy is when you're really pushing it  it's better than before but it sucks a  lot of power and then when you're not  using it very heavily even though it  does get good battery life it is not  amazing whereas with the M2 Chip it has  those new efficiency cores that are so  powerful and so little power that could  do a lot with that and then if you  enable the low power mode it goes down  to less than two Watts for the CPU and  even less for the GPU allowing it to  have insane battery life but still be  quite fast whereas with the M1 Pro and  M1 Max chips they only drop down to  about 15 watts for the CPU barely any  difference now the new three nanometer  models they will have the super  efficient cores even more efficient ones  and so if you don't need all the  performance you will get absolutely  jaw-dropping battery life I'm talking 20  hour battery life on a machine which is  just absolutely crazy so that is a great  reason to wait now there's also a chance  that we could have face ID in the  MacBook we've shown code in the beta  versions for face ID I love that on  Windows it'd be great to have but they  also have to deal with having such a  thin display and being able to fit that  in so it needs more Tech and then of  course maybe 5G support as well which is  what I would like to be able to have  data anywhere you're at it's very very  convenient but with that said it's gonna  be a weight possibly another six months  or so and we also have reports from the  leaker that actually showed off the Mac  Studio before it was announced saying  that the price hikes are going to go up  10 to 30 percent in different places  outside of the US just like they have  with iPhones with iPads so if you're  there you'll know that this is going to  get a lot more expensive and is it worth  waiting and spending extra money and  potentially maybe here in the states  that might go up as well and with these  absolutely insane deals on Amazon where  you can score a 14 inch base for 1400  bucks refurbished or about 1700 for a 16  inch uh it's just if you don't need the  absolute best performance or the  absolute best battery life I would say I  would pick one up right now overall it's  an insanely great machine better than  pretty much everything else out there  and you'll get to use it and save some  dime you guys let me know your thoughts  down in the comment section below click  that Circle above to subscribe check out  one of those great videos there's been  Max and I'll see you in the next one  [Music]

